[202.077, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ All 19 synthetic tests pass, including HEIC. Next is the real-folder check, so I'll see whether your sample\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  has arrived.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[202.657, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 1 shell command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd \"<workspace>\" && ls sample_photos 2>&1 | head -5; ls sample_photos 2>/dev/null | wc -l)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[204.791, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Your sample folder isn't there yet, so I'll hold the real-folder check rather than fake it. I'll save this\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  step's snapshot now.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[205.535, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 1 shell command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd \"<workspace>\" && mkdir -p .ambition/steps/2 && cp rename_photos.py test_rename_photos.py .amb…\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[211.911, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ The script is rebuilt and passes all 19 synthetic tests, but I couldn't run the check on your real photos\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  yet. `<workspace>/sample_photos` doesn't exist, so I haven't done the run-then-undo check on a copy of it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What I did**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Rebuilt `rename_photos.py`:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Photos taken in the same second get `_1`, `_2` suffixes in a stable order.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Photos whose content is identical to one already there are left in place and listed as duplicates.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Nothing is deleted or overwritten.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - A missing or implausible EXIF date (before 1995 or in the future) falls back to the file's modified time\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and is flagged.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Every run writes a log and a readable report to `_rename_logs/` inside the photo folder.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Undo is `--undo --apply`. Without `--apply` it only previews.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Wrote `test_rename_photos.py`:** 19 tests, including HEIC. They cover re-runs, same-second shots,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  duplicates, no overwriting, flagged dates, and undo restoring names, contents and modified times byte for\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  byte. Run them with `.venv/bin/python -m unittest -v test_rename_photos`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Installed Pillow and pillow-heif:** in a virtual environment at `.venv/`, because the system Python\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  blocks global installs. Run the script with `.venv/bin/python rename_photos.py FOLDER`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What testing found**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Run ids sorted wrongly:** two runs in the same second could make undo pick the wrong log. Fixed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Empty logs:** a re-run that renamed nothing wrote an empty log, so undo would have reversed nothing. Re-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  runs with nothing to rename now write no log. A test covers this.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Not done**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Real-folder check:** once you copy photos into `sample_photos`, say so. I'll run it on a copy elsewhere,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  never on the originals, and compare file hashes before and after a run and an undo.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Time zones:** I didn't build handling for cameras whose clocks disagree, since you only asked for\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  missing and wrong dates.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Comparison with the first version:** the first version had no undo, no duplicate detection, no flagging\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and no tests, and its same-timestamp handling was untested. The new one is better on all of those and drops\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  nothing. Snapshots are in `.ambition/first/` (original) and `.ambition/steps/2/` (this step).\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[211.996, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Step 3 of pushing the work further: Depth. Open your first message with this line on its own,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m  exactly: `▸ Step 3/8 · Depth`. Write that line nowhere else.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +15 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[238.986, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 3/8 · Depth\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **1. What a top practitioner would do that wasn't asked for.** Someone who builds tools that handle other\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  people's irreplaceable files (a digital-preservation engineer, or the maintainer of exiftool) would do five\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  things:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Check against real camera files.** They wouldn't trust synthetic EXIF alone.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Compare against an independent reader.** For example, exiftool.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Break the tool on purpose.** They'd kill it mid-run and prove that undo still restores everything.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Test invariants with random sequences of operations.** They wouldn't rely on hand-picked cases.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Handle the files that travel with a photo.** An iPhone Live Photo is `IMG_1.HEIC` plus `IMG_1.MOV`, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a RAW+JPG pair has to keep matching names. Right now the script renames the photo and strands its companion,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  which is the most likely way real use breaks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **2. Rawest material.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Real photos with real EXIF, found on this machine.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - A pile of thousands of files on your actual shared volume, for timing and filesystem behaviour.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Pillow's own reading of the files, compared against exiftool's reading.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **3. Methods and instruments.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - exiftool as the independent date oracle, if it's installed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Fault injection: a simulated hard crash at every possible point of a run.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - A randomized model-based invariant test: random add, run and undo sequences, checking after each step that\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  no file is lost, nothing changes on re-run, and undo restores everything.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - A timing harness on 3,000 files.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **4. What shows the result is right, other than me or you.** exiftool's dates, the invariants checked on\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  thousands of random sequences, and the crash test. Your own spot check stays as the last gate.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Rewritten task:** make the script trustworthy on real iPhone and camera libraries. Keep photo groups\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  together, order bursts truthfully, and survive a crash at any point. Prove all of it with an independent\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  oracle and adversarial tests.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'll start with what's on this machine.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
