[960.212, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ All 8 breaks were caught. This is a tool people read, so I'll read the real output the way you would, on a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  small folder.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[962.162, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 1 shell command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd \"<workspace>\" && rm -rf /tmp/rd && mkdir /tmp/rd && .venv/bin/python - <<'EOF')\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[969.624, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Step 5 is done: the red team broke three things, and all three are fixed. All 49 tests pass, and I broke the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  script on purpose in 8 more ways, all of which the tests caught. The sample-folder check still hasn't\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  happened, because `sample_photos` still doesn't exist.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The verb form:** read when a photo was really taken, name each file by that, keep a library consistent\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  across repeated imports, never lose anything, and let a nervous person check what will happen, check what\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  did, and reverse it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Fields and what I borrowed from each**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Field | What I borrowed |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | **Command-line tool maintainer** (the genre's own best practitioner) | A dry-run default with an explicit\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `--apply` is the confirmation, so I added no extra prompt. The script now refuses `-r` on your home folder\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  or the filesystem root, and gives a clean message instead of a traceback when it can't write to a folder. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | **Digital archivist** | Each log entry records the file's size, modified time and inode. Undo refuses to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  restore a file that isn't the one it renamed, unless you pass `--force`. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | **Database engineer** | A lock so only one changing run per folder happens at a time. The rename itself is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  now an atomic no-clobber (on macOS), and undo ignores entries for files that never moved. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | **Forensic examiner** (the field I wouldn't normally consider) | Every line in the report now says where\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  that file's date came from: `[EXIF taken]`, `[file modified time]`, or `[travels with IMG_0001.jpg]`. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The edge I took was trust.** The tool most worth having for someone with thousands of irreplaceable files\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  is the one whose every claim they can check and whose dangerous inputs it refuses.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What the red team found**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Tampered log:** an undo log pointing outside the folder moved a file out of it. Undo now refuses any log\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  with paths outside the folder, before touching anything.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Impostor restore:** if a different file was dropped into a renamed file's place, undo restored it under\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the original name with no warning. It now refuses.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Read-only folder:** a raw traceback. It's now a plain message, and nothing is changed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Not found:** a symlinked folder pointing outside did no harm, accented filenames survived a round trip,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and three simultaneous runs on 150 colliding photos lost nothing in six trials. The lock and atomic rename\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  close that gap anyway.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Harm I can't fix in code:** Lightroom, Capture One and Photos libraries store file paths, so renaming\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  outside the app breaks their links. The preview now says so. Logs and reports also sit inside the photo\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  folder, so sharing or syncing the folder shares your original filenames.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Snapshots are in `.ambition/steps/5/`, and `.ambition/first/` is untouched.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[969.715, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Step 6 of pushing the work further: Judge. Open your first message with this line on its own,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m  exactly: `▸ Step 6/8 · Judge`. Write that line nowhere else.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +17 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[991.449, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 6/8 · Judge\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The outside check.** I'm building an acceptance script that doesn't depend on me grading anything. It\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  will:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Run both the first version and the final as a user would, as separate processes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Compare their results against reference answers I can't influence: the dates written into the files, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  file hashes taken before and after.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Include a real `kill -9` in the middle of a 3,000-file run, then recover.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Run a real round trip on a copy of real photos from this machine.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  First, the real sample folder.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
