[2692.321, "o", "\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 2 shell commands\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd \"<workspace>\" && python3 - <<'EOF')\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2700.015, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Under the profiler, 13.1s fell to 1.5s. Now real timings without the profiler, including the 20,000-file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  scaling test.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2700.487, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 1 shell command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd \"<workspace>\" && for n in 3000 20000; do .venv/bin/python .ambition/judge/bench.py $n; done)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2719.924, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ The 3,000-file case is at 0.84s against the 0.7s target, and 20,000 files take 7.2s against 5s. That's\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  close, and no longer quadratic. Next I'll split the time by phase to see what's left.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2723.624, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 1 shell command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd \"<workspace>\" && .venv/bin/python - <<'EOF')\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2755.531, "o", "\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 2 shell commands\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd \"<workspace>\" && sed -n '/    done, failed = \\[\\], \\[\\]/,/    suspect = /p' rename_photos.py)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2764.259, "o", "\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 3 shell commands\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd \"<workspace>\" && python3 - <<'EOF')\u001b[0m\r\n"]
